        {
          "path": "_m/8/e/8/z/pe-ahi-hawaii-wp/jeff-rowley-1-photo-by-minnie-.jpg",
          "filename": "Jeff Rowley 1 Photo by Minnie Vuong - Flickr - Jeff Rowley Big Wave Surfer.jpg",
          "caption": "Jaws bites - Big wave surfers, Jeff Rowley, Greg Long, Shaun Walsh and Albee Layer ‘paddle-in’ to gigantic 15 metre (50 foot) plus waves at Peahi “Jaws” and cement paddling in as the new frontier in big wave surfing.  \nRowley and friends were on Maui, Hawaii waiting for the monster surf to hit the Peahi, \"Jaws\" reef and produce the worlds biggest surfable waves.\nOn one of the biggest waves of the day, Rowley took off underneath the pitching lip of the wave. \n“As the wave was coming I knew I was in the right position, I didn't want to waste any energy paddling just turn around and go\".\n\n“It just picked me up perfectly, It felt like I was riding a magic carpet with my heart in my mouth\".",
          "alt": "Jaws bites - Big wave surfers, Jeff Rowley, Greg Long, Shaun Walsh and Albee Layer ‘paddle-in’ to gigantic 15 metre (50 foot) plus waves at Peahi “Jaws” and cement paddling in as the new frontier in big wave surfing.  \nRowley and friends were on Maui, Hawaii waiting for the monster surf to hit the Peahi, \"Jaws\" reef and produce the worlds biggest surfable waves.\nOn one of the biggest waves of the day, Rowley took off underneath the pitching lip of the wave. \n“As the wave was coming I knew I was in the right position, I didn't want to waste any energy paddling just turn around and go\".\n\n“It just picked me up perfectly, It felt like I was riding a magic carpet with my heart in my mouth\".",
          "width": 700,
          "height": 420,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Jeff Rowley",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeff_Rowley_1_Photo_by_Minnie_Vuong_-_Flickr_-_Jeff_Rowley_Big_Wave_Surfer.jpg",
